**Code Explanation:**

The code loads the data generated in Steps 2, 3, and 4 from the data/ directory and generates the six requested plots to visualize the Lagrangian tracer dispersion and chaotic vortex interactions. 1. Plot 1 (MSD): A log-log plot of the total Mean-Square Displacement (MSD) and its directional components (MSD_x, MSD_y, MSD_z) against lag time. Reference lines for Brownian (alpha=1) and ballistic (alpha=2) regimes are included. 2. Plot 2 (alpha(t)): A linear plot of the time-dependent power-law exponent alpha(t). 3. Plot 3 (PDFs): A log-log plot of the displacement probability density functions at four different lag times with fitted power-law tails. 4. Plot 4 (VACF): A plot of the normalized Velocity Autocorrelation Function. 5. Plot 5 (FTLE): A figure with two subplots: a scatter plot showing the relationship between the Finite-Time Lyapunov Exponent (FTLE) and the residence time in vortex cores (Q > 0), and a histogram showing the distribution of FTLE values. 6. Plot 6 (Q-criterion Slice): A 2D spatial map of the Q-criterion field at the z=0 slice for the final snapshot, overlaid with a scatter plot of tracers located near that slice (|z| < 0.1).

**Modifications:**

Ensured all plots are saved to the data/ directory, added the main guard, removed LaTeX rendering, and ensured all paths are correctly handled.

